WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.255 --> 00:00:15.056
Sparky raced past the judges.

2
00:00:15.076 --> 00:00:17.617
"Sparky, come back!"

3
00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:18.737
yelled Jenny.

4
00:00:19.637 --> 00:00:21.398
Josh tried to grab Sparky.

5
00:00:22.238 --> 00:00:27.039
But the hamster was so slippery from soap and water, he slipped through Josh's fingers.

6
00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:33.258
Then Sparky ran toward a judge—the one who was wearing my magic thinking box!

7
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.561
The judge sneezed loudly.

8
00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:41.945
"Ah-choo!" She sneezed so hard that the box flew off her head.

9
00:00:42.826 --> 00:00:44.908
It landed right on top of Sparky!

10
00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:48.090
Sparky was scared.

11
00:00:48.871 --> 00:00:51.173
He didn't like being trapped in a dark box.

12
00:00:53.355 --> 00:00:54.916
So he ran faster than ever.

13
00:00:54.936 --> 00:00:58.219
"Ha-ha! Look at that box!"

14
00:00:58.699 --> 00:00:59.760
One of the kids laughed.

15
00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:01.532
"It has legs!"

16
00:01:02.473 --> 00:01:03.533
The boy was right.

17
00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:07.815
Sparky's legs stuck out as the box moved across the floor.

18
00:01:08.775 --> 00:01:11.216
It looked like the box was running all by itself!

19
00:01:13.037 --> 00:01:16.599
Soon all the kids were laughing as Sparky raced around the big room.

20
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.240
Even the judges laughed.

21
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:26.162
The judge who had tried out my magic thinking box laughed the hardest of all.

22
00:01:27.123 --> 00:01:29.624
Sparky raced under a table and knocked it over.

23
00:01:30.776 --> 00:01:35.838
Finally Josh caught up with him, and he lifted the magic thinking box off his hamster.

24
00:01:35.858 --> 00:01:38.339
"Sparky!" he said.

25
00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.200
"I'm so glad I caught you!"

26
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.302
I ran up to Josh, and a group of kids followed me.

27
00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:48.623
"I bet I know what Sparky was thinking," I said.

28
00:01:48.643 --> 00:01:51.945
"What?" a bunch of kids asked.

29
00:01:52.925 --> 00:01:55.026
"Sparky was probably thinking, 'Help!

30
00:01:55.386 --> 00:01:58.967
Get me out of this box!'"

31
00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:02.453
Some kids laughed, but I sighed.

32
00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:07.334
I might be right about Sparky's thoughts, but I wasn't going to win a prize.

33
00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:12.315
I hadn't even had a chance to show the judges how my invention worked.

34
00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:16.336
Soon it was time for the judges to choose the winners.

35
00:02:17.697 --> 00:02:19.577
One judge announced third prize.

36
00:02:21.638 --> 00:02:25.859
A boy who had invented a bicycle fan to keep him cool on hot days won that.

37
00:02:26.899 --> 00:02:29.260
Next the judge announced second prize.

38
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:38.902
"This prize goes to Susie Johnson for inventing a new use for old CDs—wearing them as earrings!"

39
00:02:42.463 --> 00:02:45.964
All the kids clapped as Susie went up to claim the red ribbon.

40
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:50.566
Everyone waited for the judge to announce first prize.

41
00:02:50.586 --> 00:02:58.248
"First prize and one hundred dollars goes to Jenny Chen for her hamster bath!"

42
00:03:02.306 --> 00:03:05.268
The kids shouted and whistled as Jenny accepted the money.

43
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.852
The judge put a big blue ribbon on Sparky's cage.

44
00:03:11.853 --> 00:03:12.974
I was happy for Jenny.

45
00:03:13.755 --> 00:03:14.735
She deserved to win.

46
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:16.697
But I was sad for me.

47
00:03:17.577 --> 00:03:19.919
It was clear that I wasn't a very good inventor.

48
00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.761
I hadn't even won third prize.

49
00:03:24.562 --> 00:03:29.321
When we got back to our apartment building, I told my mom about the Invention Convention.

50
00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:34.402
"Jenny won first prize and one hundred dollars," I said.

51
00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:36.863
"That's wonderful!"

52
00:03:37.243 --> 00:03:37.883
Mom said.

53
00:03:37.903 --> 00:03:40.564
"I know," I said.

54
00:03:41.044 --> 00:03:41.744
I looked down.

55
00:03:41.764 --> 00:03:46.405
"But I was hoping to win so you wouldn't have to rob a bank."

56
00:03:47.446 --> 00:03:49.986
"What?" Mom looked totally shocked.

57
00:03:50.947 --> 00:03:53.227
Tate came out of our room to see what was going on.

58
00:03:53.247 --> 00:03:55.888
"Wait a minute, Iggy!"

59
00:03:56.252 --> 00:03:56.872
Mom said.

60
00:03:56.892 --> 00:03:59.113
"I'm thrilled Jenny won.

61
00:03:59.574 --> 00:04:01.914
But what did you say about me robbing a bank?"

62
00:04:01.935 --> 00:04:05.436
"Don't listen to Iggy, Mom," said Tate.

63
00:04:05.456 --> 00:04:07.757
"He's just inventing stories."

64
00:04:07.777 --> 00:04:11.979
"But I heard you on the phone," I said to Mom.

65
00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:14.680
"You said you would have to rob a bank!"

66
00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.222
My mom frowned, trying to recall what I was talking about.

67
00:04:19.242 --> 00:04:22.503
"Oh, I remember!"

68
00:04:23.103 --> 00:04:24.024
she said at last.

69
00:04:24.972 --> 00:04:26.394
Then she looked at me and sighed.

70
00:04:26.414 --> 00:04:30.258
"Iggy," she said.

71
00:04:30.278 --> 00:04:31.940
"You'd better sit down.

72
00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.321
You too, Tate."

73
00:04:34.783 --> 00:04:36.345
"Uh-oh," I thought.

74
00:04:37.106 --> 00:04:39.028
We were about to find out something.

75
00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:42.391
And it sounded like it was something bad.
